\begin{scripture}[][noindent]
  \vs{50}Jesus said, “You believe because I told you I saw you under the fig
  tree. You will see greater things than that.” \vs{51}He then added, “Very
  truly I tell you, you will see ‘heaven open, and the angels of God ascending
  and descending on’ the Son of Man.”

  \ch{2}On the third day a wedding took place at Cana in Galilee. Jesus’
  mother was there, \vs{2}and Jesus and his disciples had also been invited to
  the wedding. \vs{3}When the wine was gone, Jesus’ mother said to him, “They
  have no more wine.”
\end{scripture}

\begin{scripture}
  \begin{poetry}
    \vs{11}“Also for you, Judah,
    a harvest is appointed.

    “Whenever I would restore the fortunes of my people,

    \ch{7}whenever I would heal Israel,
    the sins of Ephraim are exposed

    and the crimes of Samaria revealed.
    They practice deceit,
    thieves break into houses,
    bandits rob in the streets;
  \end{poetry}
